# NPS-DEV-POLICY: "Development Policy, Gettysburg National Military Park (Farm Lands and Farm Structures)", memorandum for the Director of November 14, 1938, approved by Director Arno B. Cammerer on December 9, 1938, and sent to the regional directors in January 1939 (a scanned typescript of 5 pages; its text layer is a damaged OCR).
# Quotes are typed as the PAGE IMAGES of PDF pp. 2 and 3 read (looked at 2026-11-16; the digit of 'the present 18 farms' was enlarged: the OCR reads 16, the page reads 18) and aligned to the OCR text of scripts/ocr.py by scripts/ocrq.py.
# This is a statement of 1938 conditions and of policy, not of 1863: every extract is use indirect (the farms as leased in 1938) or none (structures put up after the battle), except where the memorandum itself says a structure stands as it did at the time of the battle.
@ NPS-DEV-POLICY
%images 2, 3

2 | fields | In 1938 the farm lands and farm structures of the park were judged unsatisfactory for historical presentation and preservation, economy of operation and the lack of modern utilities | - | ~1938 (the memorandum of November 14, 1938; the condition of the farm lands then, not in 1863) | stated | The memorandum says the present conditions and maintenance of the farm lands and structures that make up portions of the park were unsatisfactory from the standpoint of historical presentation and preservation, economy of operation as farm units, and the absence of utilities for living accommodations and sanitary requirements considered essential for modern dwellings | @@It is agreed that the present conditions and maintenance of farm lands and structures that comprise portions of Gettysburg National Military Park are unsatisfactory from the standpoint of historical presentation and preservation, economy of operation as farm units, and in the absence of utilities for living accommodations and sanitary requirements considered essential for modern dwellings.
2 | fields | The memorandum blames the condition of 1938 on the operation of the farms without regard to their historic significance and on the depletion of the soil by over cultivation | - | ~1938 (soil depletion by over cultivation up to 1938; the memorandum gives no 1863 condition) | stated | The memorandum says the condition was brought about through the operation of the farms without due consideration to their historic and economic significance and the depletion of the soil with over cultivation | @@This condition has been brought about through the operation of these farms without due consideration to their historic and economic significance, the depletion of the soil with over cultivation, and in the erection of auxiliary farm structures without adequate planning previous to erection.
2 | buildings | Auxiliary farm structures were erected on the park's farms without adequate planning (before 1938) | - | !after July 1863 (auxiliary farm structures erected before 1938; the memorandum names none and gives no dates) | stated | The memorandum says the condition of the farms was brought about partly by the erection of auxiliary farm structures without adequate planning previous to erection | @@This condition has been brought about through the operation of these farms without due consideration to their historic and economic significance, the depletion of the soil with over cultivation, and in the erection of auxiliary farm structures without adequate planning previous to erection.
2 | fields | Policy of 1938: an atmosphere of farms and farm land in operation to be preserved | - | ~1938 (a policy objective; not an 1863 state) | stated | The memorandum proposes as its first objective that an atmosphere of farms and farm land in operation be preserved | @@(1) That an atmosphere of farms and farm land in operation be preserved.
2 | fields | Policy of 1938: the historical features of the major sites (Pickett's Charge, Little Round Top, Culp's Hill) to be kept as nearly in their original condition as possible, whether farmed or not | - | ~1938 (a policy objective; the memorandum does not describe the original condition) | stated | The memorandum says the policy emphasizes retaining the historical features in the major sites of the park, naming Pickett's Charge, Little Round Top and Culp's Hill, in as nearly their original condition as possible, whether farmed or not | @@(2) In carrying out this policy we recognize degrees of historical importance of lands within the Park and wish particularly to emphasize retaining the historical features in the major sites within the Park (Pickett's Charge, Little Round Top, Culp's Hill, etc.) in as nearly their original condition as possible, whether farmed or not.
2 | fields | The park's farm lands in 1938 were in 18 farms (the OCR reads 16, the enlarged page image 18), to be reduced to a smaller number of economic farm units | - | ~1938 (the number of farms in the park's farm lands in 1938; not an 1863 count) | stated | The memorandum says it seems advisable to establish economic farm units by reducing the present 18 farms to a lesser number that can be economically operated | @@(3) It seems advisable to establish economic farm units by reducing the present 18 farms to a lesser number that can be economically operated. Further study will be necessary to determine the number and boundaries of any new farm arrangement.
2 | buildings | Policy of 1938: preserve all historical structures now located as they were at the time of the battle and restore them to original appearance where possible | - | ~1938 (a policy objective; it names no structure and describes no original appearance) | stated | The memorandum proposes to preserve and retain all historical structures that are now located as they were at the time of the battle and to restore them to original appearance wherever possible | @@(4) Preserve and retain all historical structures that are now located as they were at the time of the Battle and restore to original appearance wherever possible.
3 | buildings | Policy of 1938: existing non-historic structures on the farms kept in cultivation to be repaired, relocated, replaced or destroyed | - | !later than 1863 (the non-historic farm structures of 1938; none is named) | stated | The memorandum says additional structures will be built where necessary on farms retained in cultivation and that existing non-historic structures shall be repaired, relocated, replaced or destroyed to make more efficient farm groups | @@(5) Additional structures will be built where necessary on farms retained in cultivation, and existing non-historic structures shall be repaired, relocated, replaced, or destroyed to make more efficient farm groups.
3 | buildings | Policy of 1938: historical structures not needed for economic farm units to be restored as rental units; revamped farms rehabilitated with modern utilities | - | ~1938 (a policy objective; a rehabilitated dwelling with modern interior and utilities is not an 1863 state) | stated | The memorandum says all structures of historical importance not needed as units of the economic farms will be restored as rental units and that all revamped farms shall be rehabilitated, with dwellings modernized on the interior and electricity, water and sewage disposal provided | @@(6) All structures that are of historical importance and that are not considered as necessary units in the establishment of economic farm units will be restored as rental units. (7) All revamped farms shall be rehabilitated, dwellings modernized on the interior, and electricity, water, sewage disposal, etc., provided.
